# Erdős Problem #99 — continuation after the activation-orthant audit

Work in one context. Do not delegate to subagents or separate research workers.

## Objective and quantifiers

Obtain a Level I proof or disproof of Erdős Problem #99. The immediate priority is
Target A. Do not work on Target B unless a Target B theorem supplies the missing
Target A bridge.

For

\[
D(n)=\min\{\operatorname{diam}(A):A\subset\mathbb R^2,\ |A|=n,
\ |x-y|\ge1\},
\]

a proof must show that, for every sufficiently large \(n\), **every** global
minimizer contains a unit equilateral triangle. A disproof requires triangle-free
global minimizers for infinitely many cardinalities. Local, jammed, asymptotic,
KKT, or numerical examples do not settle the global quantifiers.

